## Linux overrides (Codespaces / bare-metal Linux). Included from
## ~/.gitconfig.local, which mise renders from git/gitconfig.local.tera when
## os() is "linux" and the kernel isn't WSL's. Coder workspaces reach it via
## git/gitconfig.coder.
##
## Deliberately empty of a gpg.ssh.program override: these Linux targets
## don't run the 1Password desktop app, so there's no op-ssh-sign binary to
## point at. Git 2.34+ falls back to `ssh-keygen -Y sign` for SSH commit
## signing when gpg.ssh.program is unset, which needs a real private key
## file or an ssh-agent socket available — not verified working in this
## environment; confirm commit signing actually succeeds on a fresh
## Codespace/Coder box before relying on it.
##
## WSL is detected by git/gitconfig.local.tera and gets git/gitconfig.wsl
## instead of this file.
##
## Identity block below (#81 review): starting point is an identical copy
## of git/gitconfig.darwin's values. Put a machine-specific identity in the
## untracked ~/.gitconfig instead of editing this shared file.
